Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Finder-Scope Chews the Parallax
- Story & Context: During the August 1997 Perseid meteor shower, Clara Vane lugged a dented cardboard reflector telescope and an overdriven amplifier up to the gravel roof of the Basel Botanical Greenhouse to test plant bio-voltages against celestial alignments. While she monitored the twitching microvolt signals of an electroded Amazonian philodendron, an errant short in a spliced power strip ignited a dry canvas tarp, filling the rooftop stairwell with the acrid stench of scorched asphalt and wet moss. Instead of fleeing, Clara thrust her harmonica into the green-bullet mic and wailed over Geryon Keller's chugging 130 BPM analog sequencer while campus watchmen hammered frantically on the fire escape below. Anchoring the chaos, Clara roared the track’s defining mantra directly through the blistering tape-delay feedback: "Breathe through the brass, the leaves are waking up!"
