Track 2: “Is That Mars or a Chimney Spark?”
- Story & Context: Crouched beside a cold galvanized vent on the roof above a chemical depot, Keller confessed to Clara that he had doctored three months of lab transpiration spreadsheets just to divert university grant money toward high-end analog delay pedals. He tracked distant planetary coordinates through a creaking brass amateur telescope that reeked of machine oil and soot, his hands trembling as the rolling progressive trance sub-bass shook the rooftop chimney brickwork. The track harnesses his mounting paranoia, modulating the JP-8000 pad chords whenever the chill river wind dropped the electrical resistance across their potted ficus. Across a relentless, syncopated EBM stomp, Clara delivers a deadpan spoken hook cutting through the cavernous reverb: "You stole the light just to watch the circuit drown."
