Track 3: The Solarium at St. Johann
- Story & Context: By the winter of 1999, the abandoned rooftop solarium at St. Johann had transformed into an unauthorized sanctuary where hundreds of dancers packed shoulder-to-shoulder among rotting tomato trellises to experience the band's legendary marathon sets. Dense river fog rolled off the Rhine and pressed against the cracked panes, dripping freezing condensation onto glowing amplifier tubes with a distinct, pungent hiss. When municipal bailiffs finally welded the stairwell gates shut at dawn, the sound system kept pounding unattended because the dying ivy roots continued to conduct enough stray voltage to trigger Keller’s sequencer gates. The resulting recording immortalized the scene's demise with a soaring, tear-streaked harmonica lead cutting through a massive trance build, underscored by the crowd roaring in unison: "We are the rust on the greenhouse wire."
